m/g-truc/glm/milestone/6","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/milestones/6/labels","id":173769,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTczNzY5","number":6,"title":"GLM 0.9.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":91,"state":"open","created_at":"2012-09-12T10:39:31Z","updated_at":"2019-04-02T09:34:45Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2016-09-10T20:17:34Z","updated_at":"2016-09-20T15:46:37Z","closed_at":"2016-09-11T01:05:49Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is similar to #546.\n\nAfter including the \"gtx/io.hpp\" header into NVCC-compiled code I got another handful of warnings. For example:\n\n``` cpp\nhome/sergey/third-party/glm/src/glm/gtx/io.inl(99): warning: calling a __host__ function from a __host__ __device__ function is not allowed\n          detected during:\n            instantiation of \"const FTy &glm::io::get_facet<FTy,CTy,CTr>(std::basic_ios<CTy, CTr> &) [with FTy=glm::io::format_punct<char>, CTy=char, CTr=std::char_traits<char>]\"\n```\n\nThe offending code fragment is:\n\n``` cpp\ntemplate <typename FTy, typename CTy, typename CTr>\nGLM_FUNC_QUALIFIER FTy const& get_facet(std::basic_ios<CTy, CTr>& ios)\n{\n    if(!std::has_facet<FTy>(ios.getloc()))\n        ios.imbue(std::locale(ios.getloc(), new FTy));\n    return std::use_facet<FTy>(ios.getloc());\n}\n```\n\nIndeed, functions from the Standard Library are `__host__` only. And anyway, I guess functions from the IO module are not supposed to be run on the GPU. Should we remove the `GLM_FUNC_QUALIFIER` from them?\n\n**EDIT** Actually, the functions still need to be inlined, so rather replace `GLM_FUNC_QUALIFIER` with `GLM_INLINE`.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline